      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure this is needed. `fs/exec.c` doesn\u0027t opt into `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, so `__PAGE_ALIGN()` already gives a 16KB-aligned `stack_top`, which is valid for a 4KB process, and the arg-page walk already uses `mm_pte_size(bprm-\u003emm)` at lines 454 and 565.\n\nAligning to 4KB also makes the `relocate_vma_down()` shift 4, 8 or 12KB, which I think moves anon slices off the slice their address selects until aosp/4367983 realigns them in b17. It also drops ACK\u0027s `__PAGE_ALIGN()` for the x86_64 page size emulation.\n\nIf the goal is 4KB stack ASLR, could this move next to aosp/4367982 and aosp/4367983 so that every patch stays correct on its own? Otherwise, would you be OK dropping it?",
